recommendation:
Replace the hard-coded constants with immutable constructor parameters: `constructor(..., uint256 oldNftId_, uint256 newNftIndex_)`. Add on-chain consistency checks inside migrateMint:
  require(INFTMinterV2(minter).tokenIdToDispatcher(NEW_NFT_INDEX) == address(this), 'BalancerPoolerV2: not canonical id-6 dispatcher');
  // Optionally:
  // (address oldDisp, , , bool oldDisabled) = INFTMinterV2(minter).configs(OLD_NFT_ID);
  // require(oldDisp != address(0), 'BalancerPoolerV2: old index not registered');
  // require(oldDisabled, 'BalancerPoolerV2: old index not decommissioned');

The first check (tokenIdToDispatcher == address(this)) is the highest-value addition — it ensures this contract only mints id-6 NFTs as long as it is the registered dispatcher for id 6. Once the protocol replaceDispatcher(6, ...) to a new contract, this contract's migrateMint reverts cleanly — no stranded mints.
